:13:14Z"},"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-06-06T21:31:39Z","updated_at":"2025-06-06T22:47:10Z","closed_at":"2025-06-06T22:47:10Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: 4.5dev5 and git current latest commit on master branch: 26df04377e\nNot reproducible in: 4.4.1 stable, 4.3 stable and earlier\n\n### System information\n\nArch Linux 6.14.10 - Godot (master @ 26df04377e) - Forward+ - dedicated AMD RX 580\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using `change_scene_to_file` on a `PackedScene` exported variable from a scene that inherits from another scene, I encounter the following error:\n\n```\nLoaded system CA certificates\nLoading resource: res://Scene_01.tscn\nLoading resource: res://Scene.tscn\nLoading resource: res://scene.gd\nLoading resource: res://\nFailed loading resource: res://\nERROR: Resource file not found: res:// (expected type: )\n   at: _load (core/io/resource_loader.cpp:351)\n   GDScript backtrace (most recent call first):\n       [0] _on_timer_timeout (res://scene.gd:9)\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a scene with a `Timer` and a `PackedScene` exported variable, then switch scene with `change_scene_to_file` at the `timeout` signal.\nMake two other scenes that inherits from the scene just created, and set the `next_scene` to your second scene.\n\nOnly `change_scene_to_file` causes the problem, using `change_scene_to_packed` works fine.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nMRP for reproducing the problem.\n[godot-4.5-dev-prj.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20634428/godot-4.5-dev-prj.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":""